    "transcript": {
        "duration": 33.040000915527344,
        "text": "A biologically integrated computer was just announced. A groundbreaking computer made with living human neurons is now operational at Singapore. Cortical Labs has developed a unique computer prototype that incorporates living human neurons grown from stem cells. Each unit has around 200 000 neurons on a chip that processes electrical signals, allowing the cells to adapt and respond. This biologically integrated server rack consumes only 30 watts, significantly less than traditional AI ships. While it's still a prototype, this innovation could pave the way for future applications in complex problem solving.",
